From: Holodor <holodor@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s: volume-up must not wake the system

Only the power button should wake the Odin 3 from suspend. Volume-up sits
proud on the top edge and gets pressed in a bag or case, silently waking
the device and draining it. Ported from ArmadaOS "Restrict suspend wake
sources to power and lid open" (armada-packages 6acedce, 2026-08-22).

Credit: ArmadaOS.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
@@ -117,6 +117,5 @@
 			gpios = <&pm8550_gpios 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			debounce-interval = <15>;
 			linux,can-disable;
-			wakeup-source;
 		};
 	};
